    "answer": {
      "short": "$0.02<17\\%<0.3\\dot{5}<\\frac{1}{2}<\\frac{3}{5}<75\\%<0.8<1\\frac{4}{5}$. Use a scale from $0$ to $2$; positions are shown on the number line.",
      "worked": "Convert to decimal form:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{2}&=0.5\\\\0.3\\dot{5}&=0.3555\\ldots\\\\75\\%&=0.75\\\\\\frac{3}{5}&=0.6\\\\17\\%&=0.17\\\\1\\frac{4}{5}&=1.8\\end{align*}$$\nThe other two numbers are already decimals. Order by place value:\n$$0.02<0.17<0.3555\\ldots<0.5<0.6<0.75<0.8<1.8.$$\nRewrite in the original forms:\n$$0.02<17\\%<0.3\\dot{5}<\\frac{1}{2}<\\frac{3}{5}<75\\%<0.8<1\\frac{4}{5}.$$\nUse a scale from $0$ to $2$ and place each value at its corresponding decimal position, as shown.",
